    "---\n",
    "## Task 2: Prepare the Fine-Tuning Data\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44f8f07e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A note on how the loss is computed\n",
    "\n",
    "If you concatenate a prompt and its label into one long string and train on the whole thing, by default every token in that string contributes equally to the loss (including the ~40 tokens of boilerplate prompt (which repeats almost identically across all 300 examples) and the 2-3 tokens of the actual label you care about. Since the prompt is long, easy to predict, and identical\n",
    "across nearly every example, it dominates the average loss, the model can get very good at \"predicting the next word of a fixed sentence\" while barely improving at the one thing that actually matters the right label.\n",
    "\n",
    "The fix is to **mask out the prompt tokens from the loss** using PyTorch's convention of `-100` as an \"ignore this position\" label. Only the completion which is the labl, contributes gradient signal. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "af15ccd7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if tokenizer.pad_token is None:\n",
    "    tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n",
    "\n",
    "def tokenize_with_masked_prompt(row):\n",
    "    prompt = build_prompt(row[\"text\"])\n",
    "    completion = \" \" + row[\"label\"] + tokenizer.eos_token\n",
    "\n",
    "    prompt_ids = tokenizer(prompt, add_special_tokens=False)[\"input_ids\"]\n",
    "    completion_ids = tokenizer(completion, add_special_tokens=False)[\"input_ids\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    input_ids = prompt_ids + completion_ids\n",
    "    labels = [-100] * len(prompt_ids) + completion_ids  # -100 = ignored in loss\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\"input_ids\": input_ids, \"labels\": labels}\n",
    "\n",
    "tokenized_train = [tokenize_with_masked_prompt(row) for _, row in train_df.iterrows()]\n",
    "train_dataset = Dataset.from_list(tokenized_train)"
   ]
  },
